    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Prospect was founded in 1835 and originally called Middletown until renamed in 1876.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofprospectohio.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Columbus, Hocking Valley & Toledo Railroad reached Prospect in 1876, bringing 44 daily passenger trains and freight traffic.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofprospectohio.com/history",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In March 1913 the Great Flood sent the Scioto River 9 feet above flood stage, devastating Prospect after days of heavy rain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofprospectohio.com/history",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Prospect’s first buildings were a log cabin and schoolhouse, followed by a hotel, general store, gristmill, and a doctor’s home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofprospectohio.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A brick schoolhouse built in 1884 now houses the Village Office, reflecting the town’s early investment in education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofprospectohio.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Prospect once boasted a half‑mile horse racetrack and eight medicinal springs that drew visitors from miles around.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
